Subject: ps2xRecomp: sign branches (BLEZ/BGTZ/BLTZ/BGEZ and -L/-AL) test the 64-bit GPR, as the EE does

Rule of Rose port, milestone 6: the back gate's door in the fence area (a169) never answered Cross. Its regions
have a facing check (GamMan region walk 0x1e02c8, flag 8) that wraps the angle difference with libgcc's soft-float
doubles; __subdf3 (0x275fa8) returned 6.37917 - 2pi = -15.904 (traced: 0x4019844460000000 - 0x401921fb54442d18
-> 0xc02fcedb7a22168c). _fpadd_parts 0x275cf0 takes the 64-bit fraction difference and negates it under
`bltzl $v1` (0x275e74), which the translator emitted as GPR_S32(ctx, 3) < 0: a positive 64-bit fraction whose low
word had bit 31 set was negated. The EE's sign branches compare the whole 64-bit register (EE Core Instruction Set
Manual); BEQ/BNE and SLT/SLTI/SLTU/SLTIU here already do. 32-bit results are stored sign-extended (SET_GPR_S32 and
SET_GPR_U32 both sign-extend), so 32-bit code branches the same as before.

diff --git a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_emitter.cpp b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_emitter.cpp
--- a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_emitter.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/control_flow_emitter.cpp
@@ -406,12 +406,15 @@
         case OPCODE_BNE:
         case OPCODE_BNEL:
             return fmt::format("GPR_U64(ctx, {}) != GPR_U64(ctx, {})", rsReg, rtReg);
+        // The EE's sign branches test the whole 64-bit GPR (EE Core Instruction Set Manual, BLEZ/BGTZ/BLTZ/BGEZ:
+        // "GPR[rs] < 0" on 64-bit registers), like BEQ/BNE above. 32-bit results are kept sign-extended
+        // (SET_GPR_S32/U32), so this only differs for 64-bit values, e.g. libgcc's soft-float fractions.
         case OPCODE_BLEZ:
         case OPCODE_BLEZL:
-            return fmt::format("GPR_S32(ctx, {}) <= 0", rsReg);
+            return fmt::format("GPR_S64(ctx, {}) <= 0", rsReg);
         case OPCODE_BGTZ:
         case OPCODE_BGTZL:
-            return fmt::format("GPR_S32(ctx, {}) > 0", rsReg);
+            return fmt::format("GPR_S64(ctx, {}) > 0", rsReg);
         case OPCODE_REGIMM:
             switch (m_branchInst.rt)
             {
@@ -419,12 +422,12 @@
             case REGIMM_BLTZL:
             case REGIMM_BLTZAL:
             case REGIMM_BLTZALL:
-                return fmt::format("GPR_S32(ctx, {}) < 0", rsReg);
+                return fmt::format("GPR_S64(ctx, {}) < 0", rsReg);
             case REGIMM_BGEZ:
             case REGIMM_BGEZL:
             case REGIMM_BGEZAL:
             case REGIMM_BGEZALL:
-                return fmt::format("GPR_S32(ctx, {}) >= 0", rsReg);
+                return fmt::format("GPR_S64(ctx, {}) >= 0", rsReg);
             default:
                 return "false";
             }
